      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:5:24:5",
      "text": [
        " لَيْسَ فِي مَالِ الْمُكَاتَبِ زَكَاةٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Muhammad Bin Khalid, from Abu Al Bakhtary, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘There is no <span class=\"iTxt\">Zakāt</span> regarding the wealth of the contracted slaves’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn al-Khashshab from Ali ibn al-Husayn from Muhammad ibn abu Hamzah from ‘Abd Allah ibn Sinan who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of a slave who has an asset; if there is Zakat on it. He (the Imam) said, ‘No, Zakat is not due on it.’ I then asked, ‘Is his owner required to pay Zakat?’ He (the Imam) said, ‘No, because it (asset) cannot go to his owner and it is not for the slave.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
